# An or is read as a sum when no bit can be set on both sides, by the
# bits each affine form may set: the low bits a part that is a multiple
# of 2^k leaves to a bounded remainder, and the bits a bounded sum spans.
# A bitwise or that is no sum, and an or with an unbound parameter, stay
# unknown; bound to 1, the parameter is below 16·%tid.x's lowest bit.
RUN: %ptxroof analyze %fixtures/micro/or_disjoint.ptx | FileCheck --check-prefix=FREE "%s"
RUN: %ptxroof analyze %fixtures/micro/or_disjoint.ptx --bind 1:n=1 | FileCheck --check-prefix=BOUND "%s"
FREE: kernel micro_or_rope
FREE: st.global.u32  global store 4 B  warp: 1–2 sectors (ideal 1)
FREE-SAME: [256 * %ctaid.x + 4 * (⌊%tid.x/8⌋ mod 16) + param_0 + 64]
FREE: kernel micro_or_uniform
FREE: st.global.u32  global store 4 B  warp: 2–3 sectors (ideal 2)
FREE-SAME: [4 * (%tid.x mod 16) + 256 * uniform(%r3@60) + param_0 + 64]
FREE: kernel micro_or_ctaids
FREE: st.global.u32  global store 4 B  warp: 1 sector (ideal 1)
FREE-SAME: [16384 * %ctaid.x + 16384 * %ctaid.y + 256 * (⌊%tid.x/64⌋ mod 2) + param_0 + 512]
FREE: kernel micro_or_wide
FREE: st.global.u32  global store 4 B  warp: 1 sector (ideal 1)
FREE-SAME: [64 * %ctaid.x + param_0 + 32]
FREE: kernel micro_or_param
FREE: st.global.u32  global store 4 B
FREE-SAME: unknown: or whose sides may both set bit 4
FREE: kernel micro_or_overlap
FREE: st.global.u32  global store 4 B
FREE-SAME: unknown: or whose sides may both set bit 7
BOUND: kernel micro_or_param
BOUND: st.global.u32  global store 4 B  warp: 32 sectors (ideal 4)
BOUND-SAME: [64 * %tid.x + param_0 + 4]
BOUND: kernel micro_or_overlap
BOUND: st.global.u32  global store 4 B
BOUND-SAME: unknown: or whose sides may both set bit 7
